  "prompt": "Are doctors' professional fees subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "d71b913ddf39726234dd02d858fac3e5275e865b",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre doctors' professional fees subject to Value-Added Tax (VAT)?\n\n### Short Answer\nDoctors' professional fees are generally subject to VAT unless specifically exempted under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, doctors who are VAT-registered must charge VAT on their professional fees unless they qualify for an exemption under the law. It is essential for medical practitioners to assess their VAT registration status and ensure compliance with the VAT regulations to avoid potential penalties. If a doctor provides services that are exempt from VAT, they must maintain proper documentation to support their exemption claim.",
